  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Trailing from the second inning, they fought back but couldn't finish it.",
    "what_this_means": "They had the formula. Giolito lasted four innings and gave up four runs early, but the bullpen held. Kyle Hart struck out two in the ninth without incident, and Marinaccio matched that clean frame. The lineup scraped together nine hits and three runs driven in, which should have been enough. But Bogaerts went 2-for-3 with a knock, and Song delivered an RBI. Neither could push it across the finish line. Three runners scored in runners-in-scoring-position situations. Nine runners remained. That's the razor's edge this team lives on. You don't lose games like this by accident. You lose them because one swing never comes.",
    "what_to_watch": "Atlanta arrives tonight with Grant Holmes on the mound. He carries a 4.33 ERA into a ballpark where the Padres haven't solved their sixth-inning timing issues yet. Michael King takes the ball for the Padres. The math on one-run results doesn't improve if the bats stay this quiet.",
